/*
------------------------------------------------------------
Problem    : Reverse Integer
Platform   : LeetCode
Topic      : Math
Difficulty : Medium

Problem:
Given a signed 32-bit integer, reverse its digits. Return
0 if the reversed integer overflows the signed 32-bit
integer range.

Approach:
Extract the last digit of the integer one by one using the
modulus operator and append it to the reversed number.

After extracting a digit, remove it from the original number
by performing integer division by 10. Repeat this process
until all digits have been processed.

Finally, check whether the reversed number lies within the
32-bit signed integer range. If it overflows, return 0.

Why does this work?

Every iteration extracts exactly one digit from the original
number and appends it to the end of the reversed number.
This reconstructs the digits in reverse order while
preserving their relative positions.

The overflow check ensures that only valid 32-bit integers
are returned.

Algorithm:
1. Initialize the reversed number as 0.
2. Extract the last digit using the modulus operator.
3. Append the digit to the reversed number.
4. Remove the last digit from the original number.
5. Repeat until the original number becomes 0.
6. If the reversed number exceeds the 32-bit signed integer
   range, return 0.
7. Otherwise, return the reversed number.

Time Complexity : O(log₁₀(n))

Reason:
One iteration is performed for each digit of the integer.

Space Complexity : O(1)

Reason:
Only a few variables are used regardless of the input size.

------------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int reverse(int x) {

        // Stores the reversed integer.
        long long reversedNumber = 0;

        // Reverse the digits one by one.
        while (x != 0) {

            // Extract the last digit.
            int digit = x % 10;

            // Append the extracted digit.
            reversedNumber = reversedNumber * 10 + digit;

            // Remove the last digit.
            x /= 10;
        }

        // Return 0 if the reversed integer overflows.
        if (reversedNumber > INT_MAX || reversedNumber < INT_MIN) {
            return 0;
        }

        return static_cast<int>(reversedNumber);
    }
};
